### Block 7 - LAZY, N+1 and fetch plans
### Select the "local" environment. Seed enough data to feel the problem: more sales = more queries.

### More data: 20 customers x 5 sales x 3 items = 100 sales
POST {{host}}/admin/seed?customers=20&products=10&salesPerCustomer=5&itemsPerSale=3

### THE PROBLEM: one listing, how many SQL statements?
### Q: how does the number grow when we add more sales?
GET {{host}}/demo/fetch/n-plus-one

### FIX 1: fetch plan declared with @EntityGraph (SaleRepository.findAllWithEntityGraph)
GET {{host}}/demo/fetch/entity-graph

### FIX 2: fetch plan written in the query (SaleRepository.findAllJoinFetch)
### Q: why "left join fetch" and why "distinct"?
GET {{host}}/demo/fetch/join-fetch

### LAZY is not magic: getReference() gives a proxy, SQL only when you read a property
### Q: which call finally triggers the SELECT?
GET {{host}}/demo/lazy/proxy?productId={{productId}}

### The classic error: reading a LAZY association after the transaction ended
### Q: why does it work in the listing but fail here? (open-in-view is off)
GET {{host}}/demo/lazy/outside-tx?saleId={{saleId}}
